<p><strong>Pinnacle Sales has partnered with <a href="/brands/us-stone-group/">US Stone Group</a> to distribute luxury stone and surfaces across the Western U.S.</strong> It's a first for us on two fronts: our first surfaces line, and our first true distribution partnership. For our dealers, it means the countertop and the cabinetry can now come from the same rep.</p>

<h2>Who is US Stone Group</h2>
<p>Based in Westminster, California, US Stone Group is a luxury stone and surface supplier that hand-selects premium natural stone, porcelain, and semi-precious gemstone slabs from the world's finest quarries. The team holds quarry-direct relationships with the owners of the Cristallo and Patagonia quartzite quarries, backed by a 20-year global sourcing network — so the inventory leans toward rare, visually distinctive material rather than commodity stone.</p>

<h2>What's now available through Pinnacle</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Natural stone</strong> — quartzite, marble, granite, and travertine, including the signature Cristallo and Patagonia lines plus Taj Mahal, Mont Blanc, Perla Venata, and Emerald. Available in 2 cm and 3 cm.</li>
  <li><strong>Semi-precious</strong> — agate, amethyst, crystal quartz, sodalite, and decorative mineral slabs; many are translucent and backlight-ready.</li>
  <li><strong>Porcelain</strong> — large-format Italian porcelain in marble, stone, and travertine looks for floors, walls, and counters.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Why it matters for your dealership</h2>
<p>Most kitchen and bath projects need a surface. Repping US Stone Group alongside our cabinetry lines lets you keep that selection — and that margin — in house, with one point of contact for quotes, slab photos, inventory verification, and ordering. Whether your customer needs a single statement slab or you're a slab yard or fabricator buying by the container, it routes through Pinnacle.</p>

<h2>Two ways to get started</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Spec a project</strong> — browse the <a href="/brands/us-stone-group/">US Stone Group collection</a> and request a slab walk-through for your next job.</li>
  <li><strong>Buy by the container</strong> — dealers, slab yards, and fabricators can purchase full containers at quarry-direct pricing. See <a href="/playbook/us-stone-container-program/">our container program and the current Perla Venata + Cristallo container</a>.</li>
</ul>

